-Wextra -Wpointer-arith -Wwrite-strings -Wshadow -Winline -Wnested-externs -Wmissing-declarations -Wmissing-prototypes -Wno-long-long -Wfloat-equal -Wno-multichar -Wsign-compare -Wundef -Wno-format-nonliteral -Wendif-labels -Wstrict-prototypes -Wdeclaration-after-statement -Wcast-align -Wno-system-headers -Wshorten-64-to-32 -Wunused -Wvla -Wshift-sign-overflow -Wmissing-variable-declarations -Wdouble-promotion -Wcomma -Wassign-enum -Wextra-semi-stmt -Werror=partial-availability\r\n  CPPFLAGS:        -isystem [redacted path]/zlibstat/include -isystem [redacted path]/mbedtls/include -isystem [redacted path]/libssh2/include -isystem [redacted path]/nghttp2/include\r\n  LDFLAGS:         -framework CoreFoundation -framework SystemConfiguration -L[redacted path]/zlibstat/lib -framework CoreFoundation -framework Security -L[redacted path]/mbedtls/lib -L[redacted path]/libssh2/lib -L[redacted path]/nghttp2/lib\r\n  LIBS:            -lnghttp2 -lssh2 -lssh2 -lmbedtls -lmbedx509 -lmbedcrypto -lldap -lzstd -lbrotlidec -lz\r\n\r\ncurl version:     7.86.0\r\nSSL:              enabled (Secure Transport, mbedTLS)\r\nSSH:              enabled (libSSH2)\r\nzlib:             enabled\r\nbrotli:           enabled (libbrotlidec)\r\nzstd:             enabled (libzstd)\r\nGSS-API:          no      (--with-gssapi)\r\nGSASL:            no      (libgsasl not found)\r\nTLS-SRP:          no      (--enable-tls-srp)\r\nresolver:         POSIX threaded\r\nIPv6:             enabled\r\nUnix sockets:     enabled\r\nIDN:              no      (--with-{libidn2,winidn})\r\nBuild libcurl:    Shared=no, Static=yes\r\nBuilt-in manual:  no      (--enable-manual)\r\n--libcurl option: enabled (--disable-libcurl-option)\r\nVerbose errors:   enabled (--disable-verbose)\r\nCode coverage:    disabled\r\nSSPI:             no      (--enable-sspi)\r\nca cert bundle:   no\r\nca cert path:     no\r\nca fallback:      no\r\nLDAP:             enabled (OpenLDAP)\r\nLDAPS:            enabled\r\nRTSP:             no      (--enable-rtsp)\r\nRTMP:             no      (--with-librtmp)\r\nPSL:              no      (libpsl not found)\r\nAlt-svc:          enabled (--disable-alt-svc)\r\nHeaders API:      enabled (--disable-headers-api)\r\nHSTS:             enabled (--disable-hsts)\r\nHTTP1:            enabled (internal)\r\nHTTP2:            enabled (nghttp2)\r\nHTTP3:            no      (--with-ngtcp2, --with-quiche --with-msh3)\r\nECH:              no      (--enable-ech)\r\nWebSockets:       no      (--enable-websockets)\r\nProtocols:        FILE FTP FTPS HTTP HTTPS IMAP IMAPS LDAP LDAPS MQTT POP3 POP3S SCP SFTP SMTP SMTPS\r\nFeatures:         AsynchDNS HSTS HTTP2 IPv6 Largefile MultiSSL NTLM NTLM_WB SSL UnixSockets alt-svc brotli libz threadsafe zstd\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnce built, used `./curl --cert [redacted path]/1571753451.p12:test --verbose https://itv.mit-xperts.com/clientssl/check --cert-type 'P12'`\r\n\r\nPlease note the 1571753451.p12 in use is expired, but this does not impact the bug as the endpoint returns a 400 when the certificate is bad.\r\n\r\n### I expected the following\r\n\r\n```\r\n*   Trying 89.58.32.80:443...\r\n* Connected to itv.mit-xperts.com (89.58.32.80) port 443 (#0)\r\n* ALPN: offers h2\r\n* ALPN: offers http/1.1\r\n*  CAfile: /etc/ssl/cert.pem\r\n*  CApath: none\r\n* (304) (OUT), TLS handshake, Client hello (1):\r\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Server hello (2):\r\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Unknown (8):\r\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Request CERT (13):\r\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Certificate (11):\r\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, CERT verify (15):\r\n* (304) (IN), TLS handshake, Finished (20):\r\n* (304) (OUT), TLS handshake, Certificate (11):\r\n* (304) (OUT), TLS handshake, CERT verify (15):\r\n* (304) (OUT), TLS handshake, Finished (20):\r\n* SSL connection using TLSv1.3 / AEAD-AES256-GCM-SHA384\r\n* ALPN: server accepted h2\r\n* Server certificate:\r\n*  subject: CN=itv.mit-xperts.com\r\n*  start date: Nov 19 16:41:36 2022 GMT\r\n*  expire date: Feb 17 16:41:35 2023 GMT\r\n*  subjectAltName: host \"itv.mit-xperts.com\" matched cert's \"itv.mit-xperts.com\"\r\n*  issuer: C=US; O=Let's Encrypt; CN=R3\r\n*  SSL certificate verify ok.\r\n* Using HTTP2, server supports multiplexing\r\n* Copying HTTP/2 data in stream buffer to connection buffer after upgrade: len=0\r\n* h2h3 [:method: GET]\r\n* h2h3 [:path: /clientssl/check]\r\n* h2h3 [:scheme: https]\r\n* h2h3 [:authority: itv.mit-xperts.com]\r\n* h2h3 [user-agent: curl/7.84.0]\r\n* h2h3 [accept: */*]\r\n* Using Stream ID: 1 (easy handle 0x7fad8480c600)\r\n> GET /clientssl/check HTTP/2\r\n> Host: itv.mit-xperts.com\r\n> user-agent: curl/7.84.0\r\n> accept: */*\r\n> \r\n* Connection state changed (MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS == 128)!\r\n< HTTP/2 400 \r\n< server: nginx/1.20.1\r\n< date: Mon, 05 Dec 2022 18:47:37 GMT\r\n< content-type: text/html\r\n< content-length: 215\r\n< \r\n<html>\r\n<head><title>400 The SSL certificate error</title></head>\r\n<body>\r\n<center><h1>400 Bad Request</h1></center>\r\n<center>The SSL certificate error</center>\r\n<hr><center>nginx/1.20.1</center>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n* Connection #0 to host itv.mit-xperts.com left intact\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Instead, I got the following\r\n\r\n```\r\n* STATE: INIT => CONNECT handle 0x7fb5ea00ec08; line 1879 (connection #-5000)\r\n* Added connection 0. The cache now contains 1 members\r\n* STATE: CONNECT => RESOLVING handle 0x7fb5ea00ec08; line 1925 (connection #0)\r\n* family0 == v4, family1 == v6\r\n*   Trying 89.58.32.80:443...\r\n* STATE: RESOLVING => CONNECTING handle 0x7fb5ea00ec08; line 2009 (connection #0)\r\n* Connected to itv.mit-xperts.com (89.58.32.80) port 443 (#0)\r\n* STATE: CONNECTING => PROTOCONNECT handle 0x7fb5ea00ec08; line 2074 (connection #0)\r\n* ALPN: offers h2\r\n* ALPN: offers http/1.1\r\n* SSL: Can't find the certificate \"[redacted path]/1571753451.p12\" and its private key in the Keychain.\r\n* multi_done: status: 58 prem: 1 done: 0\r\n* The cache now contains 0 members\r\n* Closing connection 0\r\n* Expire cleared (transfer 0x7fb5ea00ec08)\r\ncurl: (58) SSL: Can't find the certificate \"[redacted path]/1571753451.p12\" and its private key in the Keychain.\r\n```\r\n\r\n### curl/libcurl version (not working one)\r\n\r\n```\r\ncurl 7.86.0 (x86_64-apple-darwin22.1.0) libcurl/7.86.0 SecureTransport (mbedTLS/2.28.0) zlib/1.2.11 brotli/1.0.9 zstd/1.5.2 libssh2/1.10.0 nghttp2/1.48.0\r\nRelease-Date: 2022-10-26\r\nProtocols: file ftp ftps http https imap imaps ldap ldaps mqtt pop3 pop3s scp sftp smtp smtps \r\nFeatures: alt-svc AsynchDNS brotli Debug HSTS HTTP2 IPv6 Largefile libz MultiSSL NTLM NTLM_WB SSL threadsafe TrackMemory UnixSockets zstd\r\n```\r\n\r\n### curl/libcurl version (working one)\r\n\r\n```\r\ncurl 7.84.0 (x86_64-apple-darwin22.0) libcurl/7.84.0 (SecureTransport) LibreSSL/3.3.6 zlib/1.2.11 nghttp2/1.47.0\r\nRelease-Date: 2022-06-27\r\nProtocols: dict file ftp ftps gopher gophers http https imap imaps ldap ldaps mqtt pop3 pop3s rtsp smb smbs smtp smtps telnet tftp \r\nFeatures: alt-svc AsynchDNS GSS-API HSTS HTTP2 HTTPS-proxy IPv6 Kerberos Largefile libz MultiSSL NTLM NTLM_WB SPNEGO SSL threadsafe UnixSockets\r\n```\r\n\r\n### operating system\r\n\r\n`macOS Ventura Version 13.0 (22A380)`\r\n\r\n### Why is this happening?\r\n\r\nFrom what I can see, the issue originates in `CopyIdentityFromPKCS12File` in sectransp.c:\r\n\r\nFor iOS, `SecPKCS12Import` is used which automatically adds the certificate to keychain.\r\n\r\nFor macOS, we do not want the certificate to be added to keychain automatically, so `SecItemImport` is used instead.\r\n\r\nNow, if we don't have the private key in the keychain, when we call `SecIdentityCreateWithCertificate` to get the `SecIdentityRef`, it fails because it cannot find the certificate or its private key in the keychain. If either certificate or private key are in the keychain, this works flawlessly.\r\n\r\nThe dirty workaround is to default to the iOS behaviour and use `SecPKCS12Import` instead, similar to what was done in #4800.\r\n\r\nA proper workaround (although not very elegant) would be to create a temporary keychain and use `SecPKCS12Import` to get the `SecIdentityRef`, followed by a a `SecKeychainDelete` to cleanup.\r\n\r\nOthers seems to have come across this issue outside of cURL (https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/31711) and the great Quinn The Eskimo seems to have filed it as a bug (r. 25,140,029).\r\n\r\nI'm more than happy to provide the p12 certificate privately if needed, just let me know :)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/10038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/10038/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"rolfbjarne","id":249268,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0OTI2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249268?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne","html_url":"https://github.com/rolfbjarne","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolfbjarne/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-23T13:58:34Z","updated_at":"2024-05-23T13:58:34Z","source":{"type":"issue","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/macios/issues